+//! Ambient life, the new look's own (no reference behaviour): WoW Forever's woods feel lived in.
+//! A few small things move near the camera, never far from it and never many:
+//! 1. **fireflies** at dusk and night: warm green motes that drift and blink low over the grass,
+//!    more under the trees and over the water, fading in after sunset and out before dawn. They
+//!    are drawn bright enough for the bloom, and the nearest few light the ground a little
+//!    (`look::lights`, [`FireflyLights`]);
+//! 2. **falling leaves** by day: from the crowns of the trees near the camera (the doodads whose
+//!    model is a tree, [`is_tree`], the same model-path test the wind sways them by), a few at a
+//!    time, tumbling down and downwind in the wind and more as a gust passes ([`wind::gust_at`],
+//!    the shaders' own gust), landing and fading;
+//! 3. **motes in the light**: pollen and dust drifting in the air, lit only where the sun reaches
+//!    them (not behind a hill, a building or a crown, with gaps in the leaves letting shafts
+//!    through), and seen mostly toward the sun, so they sparkle in the god rays at dawn and at
+//!    golden hour and are gone in shade;
+//! 4. **butterflies** by day over open ground, a couple at a time: two flapping wings on a
+//!    wandering flight, from a sprite drawn here (1.12 has no butterfly model);
+//! 5. **the weather** (`look::weather`): rain stops the fireflies, the butterflies and the motes;
+//!    the leaves still fall, more and faster; after the rain, while the ground is wet, a few more
+//!    motes hang in the sun.
+//!
+//! Everything spawns within [`tune`]'s radii of the camera, in fixed-capacity pools allocated once
+//! ([`Life::new`]), fades in where it is born and out at the edge of its radius, so turning or
+//! walking never pops anything; nothing is drawn on the ground but a landed leaf for a moment.
+//! It all goes on the shared effect stream ([`push_life`]): the fireflies and the motes as
+//! additive glows, the leaves and the butterflies as lit alpha sprites, from one small atlas made
+//! here ([`atlas_image`]).
+//!
+//! Every tunable is in [`tune`]. `worldLife 0` ([`LookLife::on`]) turns it all off on its own;
+//! `looklife <0-3>` scales how much there is for film, `looklife grade` follows the hour again.
+//! `worldLook 0` draws none of it.
+
+use avian3d::prelude::SpatialQuery;
+use bevy::asset::RenderAssetUsages;
+use bevy::ecs::system::SystemParam;
+use bevy::image::{ImageSampler, ImageSamplerDescriptor};
+use bevy::prelude::*;
+use bevy::render::render_resource::{Extent3d, TextureDimension, TextureFormat};
+
+use super::wind::{self, WindFrame, WIND_ROWS};
+use super::{LookGrade, LookLight, SkyFrame, WeatherLook, WorldLook};
+use crate::lighting::{GameClock, WowLighting};
+use crate::particles::buffer::{
+    EffectBlend, EffectDrawSpec, EffectFog, EffectLighting, EffectQuads, EffectVertex,
+};
+use crate::view::WorldCamera;
